diff --git a/native/mgu-render/PROTOCOL.md b/native/mgu-render/PROTOCOL.md
index 80a0e31..21e486f 100644
--- a/native/mgu-render/PROTOCOL.md
+++ b/native/mgu-render/PROTOCOL.md
@@ -118,6 +118,8 @@ Client to daemon:
 | 0x4d520004 | X_PIXELS | u32 id, n (1..64), n × u32 x, y, w, h, then each rect's pixels in turn, rows top-down, packed (w × 1 or 4 bytes a row) |
 | 0x4d520005 | X_PALETTE | u32 id, 768 bytes RGB: an INDEX8 pixmap's colours, for the whole picture from now on |
 | 0x4d520006 | X_FINGERS | u32 on: every finger of a gesture in the app's claims comes as X_FINGER, with its id; TOUCH no longer comes. Off by default |
+| 0x4d520007 | X_SCENE_TEXTURE | u32 token, w, h, then RGBA8 bytes. Zero dimensions delete the texture |
+| 0x4d520008 | X_SCENE | u32 w, h, then the scene commands below |
 
 Daemon to client:
 
@@ -133,6 +135,46 @@ pixmaps count towards 64 per app and 96 MiB for all apps; pictures also
 towards 32 MiB per app. An upload past them gets an ERROR and draws nothing.
 Videos have limits of their own (below).
 
+## GPU scenes
+
+X_READY at offset 52 carries GPF1 when ready or GPF0 if the shader failed. A scene keeps an original game's GLES
+draws on the GPU, in a private RGBA8 framebuffer. X_SCENE replaces its draw
+list; op 20 (`SCENE x y w h version`) draws the result in the app's frame,
+with its placement, clip and global alpha. The version is a client-side
+change marker. Scenes are not drawn in cached layers. A driver that cannot
+compile the scene shaders omits this marker; ordinary drawing stays
+available.
+
+Texture tokens are separate from picture IDs and belong to the client.
+An upload replaces its token; use a new token when draws in the same scene
+need both versions. Upload textures before X_SCENE, then delete obsolete
+tokens. Limits: 4096 textures, 64 MiB per client and 128 MiB across clients.
+The scene framebuffer adds at most 16 MiB per client. Disconnecting frees
+all scene resources.
+
+Scene commands are little-endian 32-bit words:
+
+| Op | Words after the opcode |
+|---|---|
+| 1 CLEAR | f32 r, g, b, a |
+| 2 DRAW | u32 texture token (0 untextured), flags, source blend, destination blend, replace, vertex count; then count × f32 x, y, u, v, r, g, b, a |
+
+Positions are framebuffer pixels, top-down; UVs address top-down texture
+rows. Vertices are triangles, a multiple of three, at most 65536 per draw.
+Flags: 1 blending, 2 linear sampling, 4 repeat U, 8 repeat V; absent sampling
+flags mean nearest and clamp. Repeat works for non-power-of-two textures.
+Source blend accepts GLES ZERO, ONE, SRC_ALPHA and ONE_MINUS_SRC_ALPHA;
+destination additionally accepts SRC_COLOR. Replace 0 modulates texture by
+vertex color; 1 keeps texture color; 2 computes RGB as
+`vertex.rgb * vertex.a + texture.rgb * (1 - vertex.a)` and keeps texture
+alpha. An untextured draw uses vertex color. A missing texture skips its
+draw. Commands and all floats are validated before the current scene is
+replaced; malformed messages close the connection. The maximum scene
+message is 24 MiB. X_SCENE renders the framebuffer before accepting the
+next message, and the completed framebuffer stays cached until X_SCENE.
+Resource exhaustion or a GPU failure sends an ERROR beginning `scene GPU:`
+and keeps the connection open, so the client can switch to pixel frames.
+
 ## Video
 
 IterioDev's protocol 4, the same in the iterio and native dialects. Another
